@OOP-778 @Axionize Why do you need the implementation to be changeable here? I just want to know what your use case is.
```java
void setBlockResyncHandler(GrimUserBlockResyncHandler blockResyncHandler);
```

Additionally, there are some existing methods from CompensatedWorld which may be helpful to expose in PacketWorld:
```
    boolean isChunkLoaded(int chunkX, int chunkZ);

    double getFluidLevelAt(int x, int y, int z);

    boolean isWaterSourceBlock(int x, int y, int z);

    double getLavaFluidLevelAt(int x, int y, int z);

    double getWaterFluidLevelAt(int x, int y, int z);
```
    
Personally I think these should all be pretty stable and thus suitable to be exposed as api, however I don't have enough knowledge of Grim to know for sure. Please let me know if you want me to add these to the PR

Do you need the water and lava fluid level specifically? Or checking if something is a water source block? We can expose it just fine but since we're going to support modded blocks in the future I'm not sure about what isWaterSourceBlock() should return for liquid that extend water or something, for example.

